A/B isolation: temporarily disabled the checkShaderErrors fix (commented out the assignment) and re-profiled. Result: frame count STILL low (315 samples, same magnitude as the 300-362 seen in both post-fix runs) and p50 8.0ms (between the clean 7.3ms baseline and the 10.0ms post-fix reading) -- this proves the low-sample-count/elevated-p50 pattern is present WITH THE FIX DISABLED too, meaning it's environmental measurement drift (this long-running session has launched many headless Chromium instances across ~10+ profile runs, accumulating system load/thermal/memory pressure over hours), NOT caused by the checkShaderErrors fix. getProgramInfoLog itself is confirmed gone from every profile since the fix landed (stack-trace profile showed 611 sample hits pre-fix, 0 shader/link console errors, and the cost vanished from all subsequent top-20 lists). Fix re-enabled (removed the //AB-DISABLED marker), verified node --check passes. The measurement environment degrading over a long multi-hour session with many spawned Chromium processes is the real lesson -- absolute p50 comparisons across runs late in a long session are less trustworthy than early-session comparisons; relative disappearance of a specific named cost from the top-20 (like getProgramInfoLog here) remains a reliable signal even when absolute p50 drifts.